
# Cygwin/git-bash crash dumps. Two of these were swept into the 39748e3
# upstream-import commit by mistake; they are NOT part of GXemul 0.7.0,
# are in no object list, and are referenced by nothing.
*.stackdump
regress/__pycache__/

# GXemul builds in-tree (no VPATH). Everything below is a ./configure + make
# product. The real build trees are build/ (pmax) and WSL /tmp/gxsec-build (arc),
# but a stray in-tree build otherwise floods `git status` with ~200 entries and
# can hide a genuinely new file (a fresh regress/ probe) in the noise. None of
# these names is tracked; git never ignores an already-tracked file, so listing
# them is safe.
*.o
/config.h
/gxemul
Makefile

# Compiled code generators and build-time tools. The generator SOURCE is tracked
# as generate_*.c; the extensionless executables are products (the negation keeps
# any future generate_*.c visible).
src/cpus/generate_*
!src/cpus/generate_*.c
src/include/make_ppc_spr_strings
src/devices/fonts/Xconv_raw_to_c

# Offline differentials and reproductions build to EXTENSIONLESS executables beside
# their own source.  Two of them (regress/diff_m8820x, regress/repro_m8invread) were
# staged by a `git add regress/` on 2026-08-16 and caught only by reading the status
# output -- an ELF blob in a source tree is the kind of thing that gets committed once
# and then lives forever.  Same shape as the generate_* rule above: the SOURCE is
# tracked as *.c, the product is not, and the negation keeps any future .c visible.
regress/diff_*
!regress/diff_*.c
regress/repro_*
!regress/repro_*.c

# The dashboard is GENERATED from tools/pipeline/ledger.json by gen_dashboard.py.
# The ledger is the source of truth and IS tracked; the rendering is not, so a
# regenerate does not show up as a 480 KB diff on every commit.  Never hand-edit it.
tools/pipeline/dashboard.html
tools/pipeline/evidence/
